# Secrets: functions about a `secret(T)` (E DR-19). A secret flows through
# what forwards its content and is inspected by nothing else (E0301);
# `secret.declassify` is the one way out on purpose, with the reason, which
# `declassified/2` records (docs/reference.md, an input's refinement).
package secret

#| The value, its secret label removed; `declassified/2` records why (E DR-19).
#| example: let fingerprint = secret.declassify(key.sha, "a digest is public")
fn declassify(value: any, reason: string) -> any forwards nulls
